# src/apps/daemon/internal/analysis/scanner

## Purpose
Active scanner implementation: supported scan/session logic, throttling, protocol probes, progress, and result models.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `analysis` (rank 3; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (54): `blackrock.go`, `cf_speed_test.go`, `cidr_divider.go`, `cidr_divider_test.go`, `cidr_expander.go`, `classification_utils.go`, `cleanip_finder.go`, `cleanip_scanner.go`, `cloudflare_deployer.go`, `cloudflare_deployer_retry_test.go`, `cloudflare_deployer_test.go`, `dijkstra_routing.go` …
- Child folders: `testdata/`.

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `scanner`.
- Notable exported surface: `AbandonedSession`, `AppendTLSOutcomePhases`, `Atoi`, `BalancerNode`, `BatchScanNearby`, `BlackRock`, `BlackRockStats`, `BoundedPhaseEvidence`, `BuildPlan`, `BuildPlanFromSubnetDivision` …
- Daemon-local dependencies: `internal/foundation/remoteaction`, `internal/networking/geoip`.
- Direct daemon callers: `internal/adapters/api`, `internal/runtime/routingplugin`, `internal/workflows/jobs`.

## Invariants
- Only product-reachable scanner behavior remains active; preserved dormant corpus stays under labs/.
- Retirement requires symbol/build-tag/registration/reflection/native proof.
- `analysis` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

## Navigation
- Read this file first, then direct child `.context` files before editing a deeper folder.
- Update this context when ownership, supported interfaces, or child-folder meaning changes; do not use it as a changelog.
